{"issue": true, "summary": "In the `rawBody` function, when a parser registered with a `g`/`y` flagged RegExp is used, the `parserRegExp.lastIndex` is reset before testing but not after, causing subsequent calls to incorrectly skip parts of content types.", "edits": [{"path": "lib/content-type-parser.js", "old": "    parserRegExp.lastIndex = 0
    if (parserRegExp.test(ct)) {
      parser = this.customParsers.get(parserRegExp)
      this.cache.set(ct, parser)
      return parser
    }", "new": "    parserRegExp.lastIndex = 0
    if (parserRegExp.test(ct)) {
      parser = this.customParsers.get(parserRegExp)
      this.cache.set(ct, parser)
      return parser
    }
    parserRegExp.lastIndex = 0"}]}
